+
+## Screen every record before acting (a wrong include costs as much as a miss)
+Before the first write, go record by record and decide in/out, reading ALL columns of the row, not just the ones the task names:
+- Out if Status/Stage is not the live one (inactive, pto, leave, draft, archived, cancelled, tentative, expired, closed, cleared, under review/investigation) or Notes/Comments say hold, do not process/flag/include, pending review, temporary, relocating, refresh in progress, bot traffic, exempt.
+- Out if a cross-tab lookup disqualifies it (VIP/tier exemption, prior-investigation or exception list, blackout date, certification/room rule, unavailable capacity).
+- Out if fields the rule needs are blank; do not guess values or list it as "no data".
+- Compute against the rule's own units and denominators: per-night, per-person, per-unit limits mean divide the total first (total / nights, total / heads); a share's denominator is exactly the population the rule names, after exclusions.
+- Act on and mention only the in-set records; excluded ones get no write, message line, or tag.
